--- OVERVIEW: LFER ---

Free-energy (LFER -- Linear Free Energy Relationship) study of pyrophosphate hydrolysis
across the protonation / Mg2+-coordination series, synced from MareNostrum 5
(supervisor's account uv169161, reserved area
/gpfs/scratch/uv36/adrian/deepmd-training/LFER). Last sync: 10/10/2026.

Three systems, same pipeline shape in each (OPES -> steered MD -> umbrella sampling -> WHAM):

  LFER_3_mg2/pph4/     H4P2O7, fully protonated
  LFER_3_mg2/pph3/     H3P2O7(-), alpha and beta isomers
  LFER_3_mg2/ppimg2/   2Mg(2+)[P2O7](4-), the bimagnesium complex
  NNP_LFER_choice/     committee-consistency check, same PMF rebuilt three times

WHAT IS HERE AND WHAT IS NOT

Only the resulting plots, the analysis scripts and the per-folder READMEs are kept. The
umbrella-sampling and SMD trajectories, the COLVAR/KERNELS files, the per-window LAMMPS
starting configurations and the trained graph_*.pb NNP models all remain on the cluster
only -- together they are roughly 884 GB, against 71 MB here.

DEDUPLICATION -- IMPORTANT WHEN COMPARING WITH THE CLUSTER

The cluster tree replicates the same job script into every umbrella window, so the
curated file set there is 8575 files but only 710 distinct ones. Only the distinct files
are committed here, each once, at the shallowest directory that covers all the places it
appeared on the cluster. Worst cases: 'job_lammps-deepmd.sh' existed in 4849 identical
copies and 'convert_restart_to_lmp.py' in 83. So if a script appears here one level above
where you expect it, that is why -- it was identical in every window below that point.
Content was compared by MD5, and no two distinct files were allowed to collapse onto the
same path.

NOTE ON PATHS

Until 10/10/2026 this folder was called 'Train_PPiMg2_LFER/', because on the cluster the
study used to live under Train_PPiMg2/. The two duplicate copies there were merged into a
single tree under LFER/ on 02/10 and 07/10/2026, and Train_PPiMg2/LFER_3_mg2 and
Train_PPiMg2/NNP_LFER_choice are now only symlinks. Repo paths again match cluster paths
one-to-one. See docs/STRUCTURE_OVERVIEW.md.

